# Copy to BOTH files — they are read by different runtimes:
#   .env       → Node tooling (astro sync, eslint, prettier)
#   .dev.vars  → Cloudflare workerd, which is what `npm run dev` actually runs on
# Both are gitignored. workerd does NOT read .env.
#
# Local Supabase (`npx supabase start`) prints these; the hosted project has them
# under Settings → API. Use the `anon` / public key, never the service-role key.
#
# For deployed environments these are NOT read from a file — set them with:
#   npx wrangler secret put SUPABASE_URL
#   npx wrangler secret put SUPABASE_KEY
#
# Both are declared `optional: true` in astro.config.mjs, so a build and a deploy
# SUCCEED without them and serve a silently auth-disabled site. See
# context/deployment/deploy-plan.md, Phase 5.

SUPABASE_URL=###
SUPABASE_KEY=###

# Cloudflare AI Gateway — receipt parsing (S-06). Same optional-by-design shape
# as the Supabase pair above: without them the app still boots and builds,
# /api/receipts/parse answers 503, and the red config banner names the feature
# that is switched off. A green deploy is not evidence these resolved.
#
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID is NOT the CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID GitHub repo variable — that one
# is build-time only and unreadable from inside the Worker.
#
# CF_AI_TOKEN is a Cloudflare API token with AI Gateway Run permission. The
# gateway itself must be named to match RECEIPT_GATEWAY_ID in
# src/lib/services/receipts.ts, with third-party (Unified Billing) credit funded
# on that gateway — the auto-created `default` gateway has it switched off.
#
# For deployed environments:
#   npx wrangler secret put CF_AI_TOKEN
#   npx wrangler secret put CF_ACCOUNT_ID

CF_AI_TOKEN=###
CF_ACCOUNT_ID=###

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright E2E (`npm run test:e2e`). LOCAL TOOLING ONLY — read by the Node
# test runner (tests/e2e/auth.setup.ts, playwright.config.ts), never by the app.
# They belong in .env only; workerd has no use for them, and no deployed
# environment should ever have them set.
#
# All three have working defaults, so the suite runs with none of them present.
# They are listed here because an undocumented env var is an invisible one.
#
# E2E_EMAIL / E2E_PASSWORD default to the local-only seed user from
# supabase/seed.sql, which exists solely for tests and carries an
# auth.identities row specifically so a real password sign-in works. NEVER point
# these at the demo account seeded by migration: its password is deliberately
# absent from this repo and that account exists in production.
#
# E2E_PORT defaults to 4321. Playwright pins the port and refuses to reuse an
# existing server (see the comment in playwright.config.ts) — `astro dev`
# auto-increments off 4321 when a sibling worktree holds it, and a reused server
# would silently run the whole suite against the wrong checkout. Set this to
# move out of the way of a dev server you want to keep running.

# E2E_EMAIL=rls-test-user-a@example.com
# E2E_PASSWORD=rls-test-password
# E2E_PORT=4321
